60,3,1,talk,Minato,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"- **May**: So, which of these four actually fits the fund’s rules and our broken drainage?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: Wetland Restoration seems to fit the fund’s water focus, but I worry about the upkeep burden on our small team.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"- **Victoria**: @Shizue, the boardwalks are hard surfaces, which the fund won't cover. That's a gap we can't ignore.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, the boardwalks are minor. The ponds fix the drainage crisis. Hard surfaces like the plaza would just trap more heat.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: @Shunichi, the ponds mean moving a lot of earth. With only two firms and the clay, that’s a big risk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Minato, valid risk, but the fund pays for the water work. The plaza would cost us everything out of pocket.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @May, the fund covers the water, but the boardwalks are hard surfaces. Who pays for those?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"- **Victoria**: @Shizue, that’s the trap. We’d be funding the very surfaces that failed us before, while the water work is free.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, the boardwalks are a small fraction of the cost. The plaza’s heat and drainage failure are the real financial disaster.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: @Shunichi, I worry the clay will slip during the pond digging. Can we phase it safely?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, the phasing notes say the south can be hoarded off. We can dig the ponds in stages without closing the whole park.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@May, that’s a relief. But @Shizue, if the boardwalks are hard surfaces, the fund won’t cover them. Who pays for that?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, that’s a fair point. We’d need to budget for the boardwalks separately, but the water work is the priority.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Victoria"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Victoria: @Shizue, that’s a fair point. We’d need to budget for the boardwalks separately, but the water work is the priority.""}]}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Shizue, the boardwalks are minor. The plaza’s heat and drainage failure are the real financial disaster.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: @May, phasing the south helps, but the clay still worries me. I hope the firms can manage the slip risk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Minato, the fund covers the water, so the risk is worth it. I’m voting for Wetland Restoration.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: I agree. The water work is funded, and the basin proved water features last. I vote for Wetland Restoration.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, the boardwalks are a small fraction of the cost. The plaza’s heat and drainage failure are the real financial disaster.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Victoria"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Victoria: @Shunichi, the boardwalks are a small fraction of the cost. The plaza’s heat and drainage failure are the real financial disaster.""}]}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I vote for Wetland Restoration. It works with the ground, not against it.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
